From: NixOS DTrace maintainers
Subject: runtest: restore core dump settings after root test runs

The test harness saves core_pattern and core_uses_pid before changing them,
but its cleanup condition is reversed.  Since core_pattern is normally
non-empty, direct test runs leave both system-wide settings modified.

Restore the saved values whenever they were successfully captured.

diff --git a/runtest.sh b/runtest.sh
index 8bf9b10..e750e40 100755
--- a/runtest.sh
+++ b/runtest.sh
@@ -400,9 +400,9 @@ closedown()
     for pid in ${ZAPTHESE[@]}; do
         kill -9 -- $pid
     done
-    if [[ -z $orig_core_pattern ]]; then
-        echo $orig_core_pattern > /proc/sys/kernel/core_pattern
-        echo $orig_core_uses_pid > /proc/sys/kernel/core_uses_pid
+    if [[ -n $orig_core_pattern ]]; then
+        printf '%s\n' "$orig_core_pattern" > /proc/sys/kernel/core_pattern
+        printf '%s\n' "$orig_core_uses_pid" > /proc/sys/kernel/core_uses_pid
     fi
